From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: complete continued_read; fail-fast ENABLE_REPORT salvage

v019 since8: ENABLE_REPORT salvage poll loops forever reading plen=13325
with code=0x03 on every chunk. since7/8 fixed chunk sizing (rd_chunk_size=256)
so all 52 chunks drain, but TD4150 never sends terminal STATUS_OK on the
last chunk — every chunk header stays STATUS_CONTINUED_READ (0x03).

Root cause:
1. continued_read returned success but left status_report_code=0x03, so
   salvage never saw STATUS_OK plen=0 for the 0x05 ack.
2. The 13325-byte frame is unsolicited continued-read data (config/report
   dump) queued before 0x05, not the ENABLE_REPORT response.
3. Salvage poll ran 200 iterations x 52 chunks (~30s boot delay).

Fix:
1. After payload fully consumed, normalize STATUS_CONTINUED_READ -> STATUS_OK
   (TD4150 transport-complete quirk).
2. Salvage: max 12 reads, stuck detection on repeated large plen, one 0x05
   retry after drain, then fail fast.
3. ATTN clear: stuck detection, cap at 4 reads.
4. Log continued_read first/last chunk only (not all 52).

Applies after syna-tcm-continued-read-chunk.patch.

